#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:58
msgid "Get the last scan results"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:59
msgid "Returns the results of the last website scan: the scripts found per category and the services that still need to be configured. The date is null when the site was never scanned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:70
msgid "Scan the website"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:71
msgid "Scans the homepage and the pages selected for scanning, the same as the Scan button, and saves the results. Takes a while per page; a call is limited to about 40 seconds. When a page fails or there is not enough time for every page, complete is false and nothing is saved (ask the user to scan from the admin instead). Limited to one scan every 10 minutes (1 minute after a scan that failed); use get-scan-results to read the last results."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:93
msgid "Configure the services found by the scan"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:94
msgid "Adds the services found by the last scan, with their cookies, the same as the auto-configure button on the scanner page. Configures every service the scan found when \"services\" is not sent. Turning off script blocking removes consent protection: confirm with the user first, then send \"confirm\": true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:102
msgid "Service slugs from services_needed in the scan results."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: seconds until the next scan is allowed.
#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:148
#, php-format
msgid "A scan ran recently. Try again in %d seconds, or read the last results with get-scan-results."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:172
msgid "The website could not be scanned. Please try again."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: pages scanned, 2: pages to scan.
#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-scanner.php:182
#, php-format
msgid "Only %1$d of %2$d pages could be scanned, so the results were not saved. Ask the user to run the scan from the Scan button in the WPConsent admin, which has no time limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:27
msgid "Get WPConsent settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:28
msgid "Returns the configured WPConsent settings: script and content blocking, Google Consent Mode, Clarity, GPC, consent duration, shared consent and the cookie policy page. Geolocation rules and IAB TCF can override some of these for visitors; see get-geolocation-rules and get-iab-tcf-settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:39
msgid "Update WPConsent settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:40
msgid "Updates only the WPConsent settings that are sent; everything else stays as it is. Turning off script blocking, Google Consent Mode or respect_gpc, or turning on default_allow (scripts load before consent), weakens consent protection, and turning on uninstall_data deletes all WPConsent data on uninstall: confirm these with the user first, then send \"confirm\": true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:63
msgid "Get the consent banner"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:64
msgid "Returns the configured consent banner content (texts, buttons, on/off) and design (layout, position, colors, sizes). Texts are in the site language unless \"locale\" is sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:81
msgid "Update the consent banner content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:82
#, php-format
msgid "Updates only the banner content fields that are sent: message, button texts, which buttons show and their order, logo, preferences panel and cookie policy texts (in cookie_policy_learn_more, %s is replaced by the service name). Texts are saved in the site language unless \"locale\" is sent. Turning the banner off removes consent protection: confirm with the user first, then send \"confirm\": true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:94
msgid "Update the consent banner design"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:95
msgid "Updates only the banner design fields that are sent: layout and position, colors, font size, button size, corners and style, and the floating icon. The position must fit the layout."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: banner layout, 2: allowed positions.
#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:309
#, php-format
msgid "The \"%1$s\" layout needs one of these positions: %2$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:331
msgid "Send at least one banner field to update."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:449
msgid "Turning on uninstall_data deletes all WPConsent settings, cookies and consent records when the plugin is uninstalled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:501
msgid "Send at least one setting to update."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:543
msgid "The cookie policy page must be a published page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-settings.php:618
msgid "Set to true after the user confirmed turning off consent protection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:34
msgid "Generate the cookie policy page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:35
msgid "Creates a published Cookie Policy page with default text and the list of declared cookies, and sets it as the cookie policy page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:53
msgid "Export WPConsent settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:54
msgid "Returns the WPConsent configuration in the same format as the Tools export file. Keep a copy before importing or resetting; note that importing it back does not restore everything (see import-settings)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:79
msgid "Import WPConsent settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:80
msgid "Imports a WPConsent configuration (the output of export-settings or a Tools export file), replacing the matching parts of the current configuration. It works like the Tools import, which has known limits: settings are stored as text, nested settings such as the IAB TCF publisher restrictions and declarations are emptied, HTML in translated texts is stripped, and a new Cookie Policy page is created. Export the current configuration first and confirm with the user, then send \"confirm\": true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:99
msgid "Importing replaces the current WPConsent configuration. Export it first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:108
msgid "Clear the WPConsent cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:109
msgid "Clears the cached cookie and service data so the banner and cookie policy show the latest configuration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:125
msgid "Reset WPConsent to defaults"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:126
msgid "Resets the banner texts, the names and descriptions of the Essential, Statistics and Marketing categories, and the consent preferences cookie to their defaults, like the Tools reset. Other categories, services and cookies are kept. Export the configuration first, confirm with the user, then send \"confirm\": true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:134
msgid "Resetting replaces the banner texts and the default category texts. Export the configuration first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:143
msgid "List addons and recommended plugins"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:144
msgid "Lists the plugins WPConsent recommends, and its addons when available, with whether each one is installed and active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:172
msgid "Install a recommended plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:173
msgid "Installs and activates a plugin from the list returned by list-addons (recommended). Only plugins on that list can be installed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:242
#: includes/admin/pages/class-wpconsent-admin-page-tools.php:785
msgid "Import data cannot be processed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-wpconsent-abilities-tools.php:319
msgid "Only plugins returned by list-addons (recommended) can be installed."
msgstr ""

